{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Trackers\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Trackers\/Sci"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"Trackers"}],"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Records"}],"externalID":"s:8Trackers7TrackerV7RecordsV","title":"Tracker.Records","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Records"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Records.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Trackers\/Records.swift#L28"},"extendedModule":"Trackers"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/trackers\/tracker\/records-swift.struct"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/AsyncIterator"],"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/makeAsyncIterator()"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/Element","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/Failure"],"title":"Type Aliases","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Aliases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/AsyncSequence-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Records"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The sequence ends once the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/finish()"},{"text":" is called, or its every copy is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"released, and every record before it has been read. Records tracked while nothing is reading wait in memory, without a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bound, for the next read, so none tracked before a delivery starts, or between two, is lost.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A read whose task is cancelled returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and takes nothing: the next read gets the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record it was waiting for, and every one after. A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/noOp"},{"text":" tracker’s records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"empty.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One task reads at a time. The first iterator to read holds the records until its iteration"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends or the iterator is released, as it is when its task ends. An iterator that reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"meanwhile waits its turn, logging a warning as it starts to, then reads on from the next"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record; several wait in the order they came, and one whose task is cancelled while it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"waits returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". So a delivery started right after a cancelled one has stopped, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while it is stopping, delivers every record the cancelled one didn’t read."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The records of the events a tracker tracks, in the order tracked: what a delivery reads."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct"},"references":{"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers/Tracker/Records-swift.struct/Element":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Element"}],"title":"Tracker.Records.Element","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/Element","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Element"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trackers\/tracker\/records-swift.struct\/element","role":"symbol"},"doc://Trackers/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","role":"collection","title":"Trackers","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The tracker app code tracks events with, and what it applies to each event before it is delivered: enrichers, samplers and consent.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/trackers"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers/Tracker/noOp":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tracker that drops every event, logging each one at debug level. Its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/records-swift.property","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":